Mechanism: RMSNorm drops mean-centering and the bias term and rescales activations only by their root-mean-square. This can make optimization slightly simpler and remove a small number of parameters, which might speed early convergence under a short fixed step budget. Prior evidence suggests the two norms reach comparable quality, so any loss difference in this tiny pre-norm model may be small relative to seed noise.
