Mechanism: A constant learning rate keeps the optimizer taking large steps throughout training. In a short, fixed budget where the model may still be underfit, this could speed progress compared with a cosine schedule that shrinks the step size early. Against this, without the cooldown that the literature pairs with constant schedules (not available here), the final iterates may stay noisy and not settle into a low-loss basin. So the hypothesis tests whether extra progress from a sustained learning rate outweighs the loss of end-of-training annealing.
